A second zero-denominator appears in the requested `ATTAINMENT_ONLY` ratio itself: the pooled nearest-start reference credits zero bits for one rule. The honest value for “best exceeds reference” is therefore positive infinity, while “reference below best” remains finite when the best is positive. I’m encoding these states explicitly; no numerator or selection is being altered.
apply patch
