# Multi-start demand-capped rescore — 2026-09-10

`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM` · recorded assignments only · no search rerun

The recorded 128 endpoints and 128 recorded F-best swap configurations were replayed on the same immutable world tapes, all 48 realised boundaries, `fading_quantile_alpha = 0.10`, and the original provisioning rule. No learner or policy run was performed. No sealed constant, threshold, sign, seed, horizon, price, guard, acceptance rule, control law, search grid, manifest, or optimizer setting was changed.

## Verified by running code

### Capacity parity gate

The gate was relaxed, by controller declaration before any demand-capped result existed, from exact binary64 equality to agreement within 2 ULP of each receipt value. The reason is that all nine fields that stopped the first run were exactly 1 ULP from their receipts, the signature of floating-point summation order, and `EVALPATH-2026-09-10.md` independently reports that matched full-48 realised parity is numerical but not universally binary64-identical. No other gate or input changed.

The corrected gate passed. Of 768 replayed floating receipt fields, 759 are binary64-identical, 9 differ by 1 ULP, and **0 exceed 1 ULP**; therefore 0 exceed the 2-ULP stop threshold. All 256 replayed served-count fields are exact. Configuration IDs and all 16 receipt digests also match.

| evaluated object | floating fields | binary64 exact | exactly 1 ULP | >1 ULP | >2 ULP | maximum ULP | exact served count |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| recorded endpoints | 384 | 375 | 9 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 128/128 |
| recorded F-best swaps | 384 | 384 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 128/128 |
| **all replayed** | **768** | **759** | **9** | **0** | **0** | **1** | **256/256** |

Each endpoint record then serializes every boundary, the exact rational subslot start/end, and every active user's delivered bits for that 0.640 s boundary interval. These records reconstruct per-user endpoint delivery before the 1.504 Gbit cap is applied.

### Three numerators

For each numerator, best-of-8 and best-found selection is performed only among the already recorded configurations, using that numerator's EE; it does not create or search an assignment. Best-found includes each endpoint and its already-recorded F-best swap. The frozen raw-capacity choice is also serialized separately so this reselection convention is auditable.

#### `SEALED`

| numerator | nearest-start reference EE (Mbit/J) | pooled per-anchor best-of-8 EE (Mbit/J) | pooled best found incl. recorded swaps (Mbit/J) | best found exceeds reference (denom: reference) | reference below best found (denom: best found) |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| `CAPACITY` | 34.570961 | 38.058640 | 38.356680 | 10.9506% | 9.8698% |
| `DEMAND_CAPPED` | 34.570961 | 38.058640 | 38.356680 | 10.9506% | 9.8698% |
| `ATTAINMENT_ONLY` | 0.000000 | 0.000000 | 0.000000 | undefined (0/0) | undefined (0/0) |

| numerator | pooled same-index start spread (`max/min − 1`) | maximum anchor spread (`max/min − 1`) |
|---|---:|---:|
| `CAPACITY` | 5.8464% | 30.7909% |
| `DEMAND_CAPPED` | 5.8464% | 30.7909% |
| `ATTAINMENT_ONLY` | 0.0000% | 0.0000% |

#### `MARGIN_Q`

| numerator | nearest-start reference EE (Mbit/J) | pooled per-anchor best-of-8 EE (Mbit/J) | pooled best found incl. recorded swaps (Mbit/J) | best found exceeds reference (denom: reference) | reference below best found (denom: best found) |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| `CAPACITY` | 47.120580 | 48.415713 | 48.608741 | 3.1582% | 3.0615% |
| `DEMAND_CAPPED` | 43.633671 | 45.080392 | 45.243918 | 3.6904% | 3.5590% |
| `ATTAINMENT_ONLY` | 34.035149 | 36.045675 | 36.308044 | 6.6781% | 6.2600% |

| numerator | pooled same-index start spread (`max/min − 1`) | maximum anchor spread (`max/min − 1`) |
|---|---:|---:|
| `CAPACITY` | 2.0864% | 15.5842% |
| `DEMAND_CAPPED` | 2.3158% | 16.0423% |
| `ATTAINMENT_ONLY` | 7.0948% | 28.1068% |

Direct reading: the demand cap does not bind any recorded `SEALED` user-anchor, so its capacity and demand-capped tables—including the 9.8698% headline gap—are identical. For `MARGIN_Q`, the raw-capacity-selected and demand-capped-selected best-found configurations are the same on all eight anchors; the capped counterpart is 3.5590%, so the measured headroom survives and is slightly larger than the raw-capacity 3.0615% under the best-found denominator. This remains a diagnostic on the recorded set.

Definitions:

- `CAPACITY`: sum of integrated delivered ACM-capacity bits.

- `DEMAND_CAPPED`: integrate separately for each user over 47 × 0.640 s = 30.08 s; then apply `min(user delivery, 50 Mbit/s × 30.08 s)` = `min(user delivery, 1.504 Gbit)`; then pool users and anchors. One user's surplus is never transferred to another.

- `ATTAINMENT_ONLY`: credit uncapped integrated ACM-capacity bits only for user-anchors whose own integrated delivery is at least 1.504 Gbit.

### Where the raw extra capacity went

Cohorts are fixed by attainment under the nearest-start reference. The comparison uses the per-anchor raw-`CAPACITY` best found among recorded endpoints and recorded F-best swaps, then sums `best-found delivery − reference delivery` within each cohort.

#### `SEALED` cohorts

| nearest-reference cohort | user-anchors | raw-capacity increment (Gbit) | share of raw increment | demand-capped increment (Gbit) |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Already attained | 0 | 0.000000 | 0.0000% | 0.000000 |
| Did not attain | 800 | 20.391788 | 100.0000% | 20.391788 |
| Total | 800 | 20.391788 | 100.0000% | 20.391788 |

No `SEALED` nearest-reference user-anchor had attained 1.504 Gbit. The cap therefore removes no delivery from either side of this comparison.

#### `MARGIN_Q` cohorts

| nearest-reference cohort | user-anchors | raw-capacity increment (Gbit) | share of raw increment | demand-capped increment (Gbit) |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Already attained | 552 | -22.453802 | 375.0406% | -4.521774 |
| Did not attain | 248 | 16.466770 | -275.0406% | 5.066705 |
| Total | 800 | -5.987032 | 100.0000% | 0.544932 |

The `MARGIN_Q` cohort quantities are signed. Relative to the nearest-start reference, the capacity-selected best found removes 22.453802 Gbit from prior attainers and adds 16.466770 Gbit to prior non-attainers, leaving a net raw change of −5.987032 Gbit. The 375.0406% and −275.0406% entries are therefore signed shares of that negative net change, not fractions of a positive surplus. After per-user capping, the same redistribution yields a net +0.544932 Gbit.

### Predeclared 2-swap subset

Before results were observed, the subset was fixed as start 0 on the first receipt-order anchor (`w1/s0`) under each rule: 2/128 endpoints. Every assignment-legal exchange was screened at the unchanged one-boundary nearest-baseline served guard, then all eligible swaps were committed over 48 boundaries and compared by strict binary64 demand-capped pooled user efficiency. These newly tested capped swaps are diagnostic only and are not fed into the headroom tables.

| rule/endpoint | legal pairs | eligible after physical validity + guard | F-improving swaps in source | demand-capped-improving swaps | not F-2-swap-optimal | not demand-capped-2-swap-optimal | best capped gain |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| `SEALED w1/s0 start 0` | 283 | 283 | 7 | 11 | yes | yes | +1.7177% |
| `MARGIN_Q w1/s0 start 0` | 605 | 605 | 10 | 26 | yes | yes | +0.8182% |
| **subset count** | — | — | — | — | **2/2** | **2/2** | — |

The original full-set statement remains a verified receipt fact—128/128 were not 2-swap optimal for one-boundary `F = B − eta_ref E`—but it is not evidence about the reporting numerator. Only the predeclared 2-endpoint subset was fully retested under demand-capped committed EE; a full 128-endpoint capped swap census was infeasible in the available run budget and was not silently replaced by a proxy.

## Derived on paper

All pooled EEs above are `sum credited bits / sum joules`, never averages of anchor EEs. `best found exceeds reference = EE_best / EE_ref − 1` (reference denominator). `reference below best found = 1 − EE_ref / EE_best` (best-found denominator). Spreads are `max/min − 1`. Cohort shares divide each signed raw-capacity cohort increment by their reconciled total.

## Inferred

The comparison measures reporting-numerator sensitivity of this recorded assignment set. It does not establish a learner-recoverable gain, a global optimum, or a sealed-result correction. Loss values were not used as evidence about EE.

